[{"input":"# Lecture 5 – Software and Machine Instructions\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\nAt the end of this lecture, students should be able to:\n- Distinguish between hardware and software.\n- Explain the different categories of software.\n- Understand how a program is translated into executable instructions.\n- Explain the concepts of source code, machine code, and assembly language.\n- Understand the roles of compilers and interpreters.\n- Read and reason about simple machine instructions.\n- Appreciate the relationship between programming languages and computer hardware.","output":"","result":"# Lecture 5 – Software and Machine Instructions\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\nAt the end of this lecture, students should be able to:\n- Distinguish between hardware and software.\n- Explain the different categories of software.\n- Understand how a program is translated into executable instructions.\n- Explain the concepts of source code, machine code, and assembly language.\n- Understand the roles of compilers and interpreters.\n- Read and reason about simple machine instructions.\n- Appreciate the relationship between programming languages and computer hardware.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"chapter\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3369-lecture-5-software-and-machine-instructions\">\n<h1>Lecture 5 – Software and Machine Instructions</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3369-learning-objectives\">\n<h1>Learning Objectives</h1>\n<p>At the end of this lecture, students should be able to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Distinguish between hardware and software.</li>\n<li>Explain the different categories of software.</li>\n<li>Understand how a program is translated into executable instructions.</li>\n<li>Explain the concepts of source code, machine code, and assembly language.</li>\n<li>Understand the roles of compilers and interpreters.</li>\n<li>Read and reason about simple machine instructions.</li>\n<li>Appreciate the relationship between programming languages and computer hardware.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"f30b48e8b4987524e9116ddb161e8fe90f7a693ef8270a37cf095c72acdfaa95","markdown":"# Cours 5 – Logiciels et instructions machine\n\n## Objectifs d'apprentissage\n\nÀ la fin de ce cours, les étudiants devraient être capables de :\n- Distinguer le matériel du logiciel.\n- Expliquer les différentes catégories de logiciels.\n- Comprendre comment un programme est traduit en instructions exécutables.\n- Expliquer les concepts de code source, de code machine et de langage assembleur.\n- Comprendre les rôles des compilateurs et des interpréteurs.\n- Lire et raisonner sur des instructions machine simples.\n- Apprécier la relation entre les langages de programmation et le matériel informatique."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"f30b48e8b4987524e9116ddb161e8fe90f7a693ef8270a37cf095c72acdfaa95","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Introduction\n\nIn Chapter 4, we studied the hardware of a computer:\n- CPU\n- Memory\n- Storage\n- Input and output devices\n\nWe learned that processors execute instructions.\n\nThis naturally leads to an important question:\n\n> Where do these instructions come from?\n\nThe answer is:\n\n```text\nSoftware\n```\n\nSoftware tells hardware what to do.\n\nWithout software, a computer would be little more than an expensive collection of electronic components.\n\nThis chapter explains how software is created and how it ultimately becomes instructions that the processor can execute.","output":"","result":"## Introduction\n\nIn Chapter 4, we studied the hardware of a computer:\n- CPU\n- Memory\n- Storage\n- Input and output devices\n\nWe learned that processors execute instructions.\n\nThis naturally leads to an important question:\n\n> Where do these instructions come from?\n\nThe answer is:\n\n```text\nSoftware\n```\n\nSoftware tells hardware what to do.\n\nWithout software, a computer would be little more than an expensive collection of electronic components.\n\nThis chapter explains how software is created and how it ultimately becomes instructions that the processor can execute.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3371-introduction\">\n<h1>Introduction</h1>\n<p>In Chapter 4, we studied the hardware of a computer:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CPU</li>\n<li>Memory</li>\n<li>Storage</li>\n<li>Input and output devices</li>\n</ul>\n<p>We learned that processors execute instructions.</p>\n<p>This naturally leads to an important question:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Where do these instructions come from?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The answer is:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Software</pre>\n<p>Software tells hardware what to do.</p>\n<p>Without software, a computer would be little more than an expensive collection of electronic components.</p>\n<p>This chapter explains how software is created and how it ultimately becomes instructions that the processor can execute.</p>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"bb4ff14c4f5a76dad31749d9d9f41bd0aaa7e23da7bb72bd03c4c54cb8cd3f27","markdown":"## Introduction\n\nAu chapitre 4, nous avons étudié le matériel d'un ordinateur :\n- Processeur\n- Mémoire\n- Stockage\n- Périphériques d'entrée et de sortie\n\nNous avons appris que les processeurs exécutent des instructions.\n\nCela nous amène naturellement à une question importante :\n\n> D'où viennent ces instructions ?\n\nLa réponse est :\n\n```text\nSoftware\n```\n\nLe logiciel indique au matériel quoi faire.\n\nSans logiciel, un ordinateur ne serait guère plus qu'un ensemble coûteux de composants électroniques.\n\nCe chapitre explique comment le logiciel est créé et comment il devient finalement des instructions que le processeur peut exécuter."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"bb4ff14c4f5a76dad31749d9d9f41bd0aaa7e23da7bb72bd03c4c54cb8cd3f27","language":"English"}},{"input":"## What Is Software?\n\nSoftware is a collection of instructions that tell a computer how to perform tasks.\n\nExamples include:\n- Web browsers\n- Games\n- Mobile apps\n- Operating systems\n- Scientific software\n- Artificial intelligence applications\n\n### Hardware versus Software\n\n#### Hardware\n\nPhysical components:\n- CPU\n- RAM\n- SSD\n- Keyboard\n- Screen\n\n#### Software\n\nInstructions and programs:\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- Chrome\n- Spotify\n- Microsoft Word\n\n### An Analogy\n\nImagine a kitchen.\n\n#### Hardware\n- Oven\n- Refrigerator\n- Cooking utensils\n\n#### Software\n- The recipes\n\nThe same kitchen can produce very different meals depending on which recipe is followed.\n\nSimilarly, the same computer can perform very different tasks depending on the software being executed.","output":"","result":"## What Is Software?\n\nSoftware is a collection of instructions that tell a computer how to perform tasks.\n\nExamples include:\n- Web browsers\n- Games\n- Mobile apps\n- Operating systems\n- Scientific software\n- Artificial intelligence applications\n\n### Hardware versus Software\n\n#### Hardware\n\nPhysical components:\n- CPU\n- RAM\n- SSD\n- Keyboard\n- Screen\n\n#### Software\n\nInstructions and programs:\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- Chrome\n- Spotify\n- Microsoft Word\n\n### An Analogy\n\nImagine a kitchen.\n\n#### Hardware\n- Oven\n- Refrigerator\n- Cooking utensils\n\n#### Software\n- The recipes\n\nThe same kitchen can produce very different meals depending on which recipe is followed.\n\nSimilarly, the same computer can perform very different tasks depending on the software being executed.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3372-what-is-software\">\n<h1>What Is Software?</h1>\n<p>Software is a collection of instructions that tell a computer how to perform tasks.</p>\n<p>Examples include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Web browsers</li>\n<li>Games</li>\n<li>Mobile apps</li>\n<li>Operating systems</li>\n<li>Scientific software</li>\n<li>Artificial intelligence applications</li>\n</ul>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3372-hardware-versus-software\">\n<h1>Hardware versus Software</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3372-hardware\">\n<h1>Hardware</h1>\n<p>Physical components:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CPU</li>\n<li>RAM</li>\n<li>SSD</li>\n<li>Keyboard</li>\n<li>Screen</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3372-software\">\n<h1>Software</h1>\n<p>Instructions and programs:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows</li>\n<li>Linux</li>\n<li>Chrome</li>\n<li>Spotify</li>\n<li>Microsoft Word</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3372-an-analogy\">\n<h1>An Analogy</h1>\n<p>Imagine a kitchen.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3372-hardware-2\">\n<h1>Hardware</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Oven</li>\n<li>Refrigerator</li>\n<li>Cooking utensils</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect3\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3372-software-2\">\n<h1>Software</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>The recipes</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The same kitchen can produce very different meals depending on which recipe is followed.</p>\n<p>Similarly, the same computer can perform very different tasks depending on the software being executed.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5037910115302d0f99dd9e80c9e6d393a4423d03aae66780008c36d06131bb18","markdown":"## Qu'est-ce qu'un logiciel ?\n\nUn logiciel est un ensemble d'instructions qui indiquent à un ordinateur comment exécuter des tâches.\n\nQuelques exemples :\n- Navigateurs web\n- Jeux\n- Applications mobiles\n- Systèmes d'exploitation\n- Logiciels scientifiques\n- Applications d'intelligence artificielle\n\n### Matériel versus logiciel\n\n#### Matériel\n\nComposants physiques :\n- CPU\n- RAM\n- SSD\n- Clavier\n- Écran\n\n#### Logiciel\n\nInstructions et programmes :\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- Chrome\n- Spotify\n- Microsoft Word\n\n### Une analogie\n\nImaginez une cuisine.\n\n#### Matériel\n- Four\n- Réfrigérateur\n- Ustensiles de cuisine\n\n#### Logiciel\n- Les recettes\n\nLa même cuisine peut produire des repas très différents selon la recette suivie.\n\nDe même, le même ordinateur peut exécuter des tâches très différentes selon le logiciel utilisé."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"5037910115302d0f99dd9e80c9e6d393a4423d03aae66780008c36d06131bb18","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Types of Software\n\n### System Software\n\nSystem software manages the computer itself.\n\nExamples:\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Android\n\nThe most important system software is the operating system.\n\n### Application Software\n\nApplication software solves specific problems for users.\n\nExamples:\n- Microsoft Word\n- Excel\n- Google Chrome\n- Adobe Photoshop\n\n### Libraries\n\nLibraries are collections of reusable software components.\n\nExamples:\n- Graphics libraries\n- Networking libraries\n- Mathematical libraries\n\n### Why Libraries Matter\n\nLibraries provide reusable building blocks.","output":"","result":"## Types of Software\n\n### System Software\n\nSystem software manages the computer itself.\n\nExamples:\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Android\n\nThe most important system software is the operating system.\n\n### Application Software\n\nApplication software solves specific problems for users.\n\nExamples:\n- Microsoft Word\n- Excel\n- Google Chrome\n- Adobe Photoshop\n\n### Libraries\n\nLibraries are collections of reusable software components.\n\nExamples:\n- Graphics libraries\n- Networking libraries\n- Mathematical libraries\n\n### Why Libraries Matter\n\nLibraries provide reusable building blocks.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3373-types-of-software\">\n<h1>Types of Software</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3373-system-software\">\n<h1>System Software</h1>\n<p>System software manages the computer itself.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows</li>\n<li>Linux</li>\n<li>macOS</li>\n<li>Android</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The most important system software is the operating system.</p>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3373-application-software\">\n<h1>Application Software</h1>\n<p>Application software solves specific problems for users.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Microsoft Word</li>\n<li>Excel</li>\n<li>Google Chrome</li>\n<li>Adobe Photoshop</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3373-libraries\">\n<h1>Libraries</h1>\n<p>Libraries are collections of reusable software components.</p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Graphics libraries</li>\n<li>Networking libraries</li>\n<li>Mathematical libraries</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3373-why-libraries-matter\">\n<h1>Why Libraries Matter</h1>\n<p>Libraries provide reusable building blocks.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"7e9b88e189168fb9af537c2de6578ceffe806064213f98ae31d7467bb2c54944","markdown":"## Types de logiciels\n\n### Logiciels système\n\nLes logiciels système gèrent l'ordinateur lui-même.\n\nExemples :\n- Windows\n- Linux\n- macOS\n- Android\n\nLe logiciel système le plus important est le système d'exploitation.\n\n### Logiciels d'application\n\nLes logiciels d'application résolvent des problèmes spécifiques pour les utilisateurs.\n\nExemples :\n- Microsoft Word\n- Excel\n- Google Chrome\n- Adobe Photoshop\n\n### Bibliothèques\n\nLes bibliothèques sont des collections de composants logiciels réutilisables.\n\nExemples :\n- Bibliothèques graphiques\n- Bibliothèques réseau\n- Bibliothèques mathématiques\n\n### Pourquoi les bibliothèques sont importantes\n\nLes bibliothèques fournissent des blocs de construction réutilisables."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"7e9b88e189168fb9af537c2de6578ceffe806064213f98ae31d7467bb2c54944","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Programs and Algorithms\n\nAn algorithm is a description of a procedure.\n\n### Example Algorithm: Making Tea\n\n1. Boil water.\n2. Place tea bag in cup.\n3. Pour water.\n4. Wait.\n5. Remove tea bag.\n\nA program is an implementation of an algorithm in a programming language.\n\n```text\nAlgorithm\n↓\nProgram\n↓\nComputer Execution\n```","output":"","result":"## Programs and Algorithms\n\nAn algorithm is a description of a procedure.\n\n### Example Algorithm: Making Tea\n\n1. Boil water.\n2. Place tea bag in cup.\n3. Pour water.\n4. Wait.\n5. Remove tea bag.\n\nA program is an implementation of an algorithm in a programming language.\n\n```text\nAlgorithm\n↓\nProgram\n↓\nComputer Execution\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3374-programs-and-algorithms\">\n<h1>Programs and Algorithms</h1>\n<p>An algorithm is a description of a procedure.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3374-example-algorithm-making-tea\">\n<h1>Example Algorithm: Making Tea</h1>\n<ol>\n<li>Boil water.</li>\n<li>Place tea bag in cup.</li>\n<li>Pour water.</li>\n<li>Wait.</li>\n<li>Remove tea bag.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>A program is an implementation of an algorithm in a programming language.</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Algorithm\n↓\nProgram\n↓\nComputer Execution</pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"f68160904ab22d40d8f3069ad4f74d8cddd7894625a77c589aea507330978ab9","markdown":"## Programmes et algorithmes\n\nUn algorithme est une description d'une procédure.\n\n### Exemple d'algorithme : préparer du thé\n\n1. Faire bouillir de l'eau.\n2. Placer un sachet de thé dans une tasse.\n3. Verser l'eau.\n4. Attendre.\n5. Retirer le sachet de thé.\n\nUn programme est une implémentation d'un algorithme dans un langage de programmation.\n\n```text\nAlgorithm\n↓\nProgram\n↓\nComputer Execution\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"f68160904ab22d40d8f3069ad4f74d8cddd7894625a77c589aea507330978ab9","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Programming Languages\n\nProgramming languages bridge the gap between humans and computers.\n\n### High-Level Languages\n\nExamples:\n- Python\n- Java\n- C#\n- JavaScript\n- C++\n\n### Example\n\n```text\ntotal = price + tax\n```\n\n### Why Not Program in Binary?\n\n```text\n01101010 11000101\n```\n\nHumans find such instructions difficult to read and write.","output":"","result":"## Programming Languages\n\nProgramming languages bridge the gap between humans and computers.\n\n### High-Level Languages\n\nExamples:\n- Python\n- Java\n- C#\n- JavaScript\n- C++\n\n### Example\n\n```text\ntotal = price + tax\n```\n\n### Why Not Program in Binary?\n\n```text\n01101010 11000101\n```\n\nHumans find such instructions difficult to read and write.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3375-programming-languages\">\n<h1>Programming Languages</h1>\n<p>Programming languages bridge the gap between humans and computers.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3375-highlevel-languages\">\n<h1>High-Level Languages</h1>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Python</li>\n<li>Java</li>\n<li>C#</li>\n<li>JavaScript</li>\n<li>C++</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3375-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">total = price + tax</pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3375-why-not-program-in-binary\">\n<h1>Why Not Program in Binary?</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">01101010 11000101</pre>\n<p>Humans find such instructions difficult to read and write.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"31ce3519f9825ef453f913f0e28c618e783221b9a14832324d10f1eb8794603d","markdown":"## Langages de programmation\n\nLes langages de programmation comblent le fossé entre les humains et les ordinateurs.\n\n### Langages de haut niveau\n\nExemples :\n- Python\n- Java\n- C#\n- JavaScript\n- C++\n\n### Exemple\n\n```text\ntotal = price + tax\n```\n\n### Pourquoi ne pas programmer en binaire ?\n\n```text\n01101010 11000101\n```\n\nLes humains trouvent ces instructions difficiles à lire et à écrire."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"31ce3519f9825ef453f913f0e28c618e783221b9a14832324d10f1eb8794603d","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Source Code\n\nSource code is the program written by a programmer.\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\nlet age = 20;\n\nif (age >= 18) {\n    console.log(\"Adult\");\n}\n```\n\nProcessors understand only machine instructions, so source code must be translated.","output":"","result":"## Source Code\n\nSource code is the program written by a programmer.\n\n### Example\n\n```javascript\nlet age = 20;\n\nif (age >= 18) {\n    console.log(\"Adult\");\n}\n```\n\nProcessors understand only machine instructions, so source code must be translated.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3376-source-code\">\n<h1>Source Code</h1>\n<p>Source code is the program written by a programmer.</p>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3376-example\">\n<h1>Example</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"javascript\">let age = 20;\n\nif (age &gt;= 18) {\n    console.log(\"Adult\");\n}</pre>\n<p>Processors understand only machine instructions, so source code must be translated.</p>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"99aa35e74cecf7074c73f570c0ccabd61fd7cb700690e1ccf04fa0e7054ad90b","markdown":"## Code source\n\nLe code source est le programme écrit par un programmeur.\n\n### Exemple\n\n```javascript\nlet age = 20;\n\nif (age >= 18) {\n    console.log(\"Adult\");\n}\n```\n\nLes processeurs ne comprennent que les instructions machine, le code source doit donc être traduit."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"99aa35e74cecf7074c73f570c0ccabd61fd7cb700690e1ccf04fa0e7054ad90b","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Machine Code\n\nMachine code is the language understood by the processor.\n\n```text\n10110011\n00010010\n11000110\n...\n```\n\n### Characteristics\n\n- Extremely precise\n- Extremely fast\n- Difficult for humans to read\n\n### CPU Execution\n\n```text\nFetch\nDecode\nExecute\n```","output":"","result":"## Machine Code\n\nMachine code is the language understood by the processor.\n\n```text\n10110011\n00010010\n11000110\n...\n```\n\n### Characteristics\n\n- Extremely precise\n- Extremely fast\n- Difficult for humans to read\n\n### CPU Execution\n\n```text\nFetch\nDecode\nExecute\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3377-machine-code\">\n<h1>Machine Code</h1>\n<p>Machine code is the language understood by the processor.</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">10110011\n00010010\n11000110\n...</pre>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3377-characteristics\">\n<h1>Characteristics</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Extremely precise</li>\n<li>Extremely fast</li>\n<li>Difficult for humans to read</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3377-cpu-execution\">\n<h1>CPU Execution</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Fetch\nDecode\nExecute</pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"e4c514e0d40909e42f7cd5bbced9d103a00ce342658fffff3f0b03e4d1364d07","markdown":"## Code Machine\n\nLe code machine est le langage compris par le processeur.\n\n```text\n10110011\n00010010\n11000110\n...\n```\n\n### Caractéristiques\n\n- Extrêmement précis\n- Extrêmement rapide\n- Difficile à lire pour les humains\n\n### Exécution par le CPU\n\n```text\nFetch\nDecode\nExecute\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"e4c514e0d40909e42f7cd5bbced9d103a00ce342658fffff3f0b03e4d1364d07","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Assembly Language\n\nAssembly language is a human-readable representation of machine code.\n\n```text\nLOAD A\nADD B\nSTORE C\n```\n\n### Advantages\n\n- Easier to read\n- Easier to write\n- Easier to debug\n\n### Disadvantages\n\n- Detailed\n- Hardware-specific\n- Time-consuming","output":"","result":"## Assembly Language\n\nAssembly language is a human-readable representation of machine code.\n\n```text\nLOAD A\nADD B\nSTORE C\n```\n\n### Advantages\n\n- Easier to read\n- Easier to write\n- Easier to debug\n\n### Disadvantages\n\n- Detailed\n- Hardware-specific\n- Time-consuming","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3378-assembly-language\">\n<h1>Assembly Language</h1>\n<p>Assembly language is a human-readable representation of machine code.</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">LOAD A\nADD B\nSTORE C</pre>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3378-advantages\">\n<h1>Advantages</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Easier to read</li>\n<li>Easier to write</li>\n<li>Easier to debug</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3378-disadvantages\">\n<h1>Disadvantages</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Detailed</li>\n<li>Hardware-specific</li>\n<li>Time-consuming</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"274e3b8b6a60584276321769e571ed9cd9b0107d940537af5ad7f7c6764a5952","markdown":"## Langage Assembleur\n\nLe langage assembleur est une représentation lisible par l'humain du code machine.\n\n```text\nLOAD A\nADD B\nSTORE C\n```\n\n### Avantages\n\n- Plus facile à lire\n- Plus facile à écrire\n- Plus facile à déboguer\n\n### Inconvénients\n\n- Détaillé\n- Spécifique au matériel\n- Chronophage"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"274e3b8b6a60584276321769e571ed9cd9b0107d940537af5ad7f7c6764a5952","language":"English"}},{"input":"## From High-Level Language to Machine Code\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nCompiler or Interpreter\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nCPU Execution\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\ntotal = 2 + 3\n```\n\nbecomes:\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```","output":"","result":"## From High-Level Language to Machine Code\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nCompiler or Interpreter\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nCPU Execution\n```\n\nExample:\n\n```text\ntotal = 2 + 3\n```\n\nbecomes:\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3379-from-highlevel-language-to-machine-code\">\n<h1>From High-Level Language to Machine Code</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Source Code\n↓\nCompiler or Interpreter\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nCPU Execution</pre>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">total = 2 + 3</pre>\n<p>becomes:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">LOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT</pre>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d01e295948c50e39ca88fd95fcd9dd6d47ea8367c1c140dfadc38d736d8e28d5","markdown":"## Du langage de haut niveau au code machine\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nCompiler or Interpreter\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nCPU Execution\n```\n\nExemple :\n\n```text\ntotal = 2 + 3\n```\n\ndevient :\n\n```text\nLOAD 2\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"d01e295948c50e39ca88fd95fcd9dd6d47ea8367c1c140dfadc38d736d8e28d5","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Compiled Languages\n\nExamples:\n- C\n- C++\n- Rust\n- Go\n\n### Compilation\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nCompiler\n↓\nExecutable Program\n```\n\nAdvantages:\n- Fast execution\n- Optimization opportunities\n\nDisadvantages:\n- Compilation takes time\n- Platform-specific executables","output":"","result":"## Compiled Languages\n\nExamples:\n- C\n- C++\n- Rust\n- Go\n\n### Compilation\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nCompiler\n↓\nExecutable Program\n```\n\nAdvantages:\n- Fast execution\n- Optimization opportunities\n\nDisadvantages:\n- Compilation takes time\n- Platform-specific executables","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3380-compiled-languages\">\n<h1>Compiled Languages</h1>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>C</li>\n<li>C++</li>\n<li>Rust</li>\n<li>Go</li>\n</ul>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3380-compilation\">\n<h1>Compilation</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Source Code\n↓\nCompiler\n↓\nExecutable Program</pre>\n<p>Advantages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fast execution</li>\n<li>Optimization opportunities</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Disadvantages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Compilation takes time</li>\n<li>Platform-specific executables</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"757e9f0d06e906b2066b44be0797dabd7f8bba370a92cbf58c97db06df28ea28","markdown":"## Langages Compilés\n\nExemples :\n- C\n- C++\n- Rust\n- Go\n\n### Compilation\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nCompiler\n↓\nExecutable Program\n```\n\nAvantages :\n- Exécution rapide\n- Opportunités d'optimisation\n\nInconvénients :\n- La compilation prend du temps\n- Exécutables spécifiques à la plateforme"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"757e9f0d06e906b2066b44be0797dabd7f8bba370a92cbf58c97db06df28ea28","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Interpreted Languages\n\nExamples:\n- Python\n- JavaScript\n\n### Interpretation\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nInterpreter\n↓\nExecution\n```\n\nAdvantages:\n- Easier experimentation\n- Faster development\n\nDisadvantages:\n- Slower execution","output":"","result":"## Interpreted Languages\n\nExamples:\n- Python\n- JavaScript\n\n### Interpretation\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nInterpreter\n↓\nExecution\n```\n\nAdvantages:\n- Easier experimentation\n- Faster development\n\nDisadvantages:\n- Slower execution","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3381-interpreted-languages\">\n<h1>Interpreted Languages</h1>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Python</li>\n<li>JavaScript</li>\n</ul>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3381-interpretation\">\n<h1>Interpretation</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Source Code\n↓\nInterpreter\n↓\nExecution</pre>\n<p>Advantages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Easier experimentation</li>\n<li>Faster development</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Disadvantages:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Slower execution</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"585047ba0c9e65b8094676aafa96daa4d76f5c943cbac92f5cd134e00cdfba1f","markdown":"## Langages interprétés\n\nExemples :\n- Python\n- JavaScript\n\n### Interprétation\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nInterpreter\n↓\nExecution\n```\n\nAvantages :\n- Expérimentation plus facile\n- Développement plus rapide\n\nInconvénients :\n- Exécution plus lente"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"585047ba0c9e65b8094676aafa96daa4d76f5c943cbac92f5cd134e00cdfba1f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Virtual Machines\n\nExample: Java\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nIntermediate Code\n↓\nVirtual Machine\n↓\nExecution\n```\n\nBenefits:\n- Greater portability\n- Same program on different operating systems","output":"","result":"## Virtual Machines\n\nExample: Java\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nIntermediate Code\n↓\nVirtual Machine\n↓\nExecution\n```\n\nBenefits:\n- Greater portability\n- Same program on different operating systems","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3382-virtual-machines\">\n<h1>Virtual Machines</h1>\n<p>Example: Java</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Source Code\n↓\nIntermediate Code\n↓\nVirtual Machine\n↓\nExecution</pre>\n<p>Benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Greater portability</li>\n<li>Same program on different operating systems</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ebae14d1aeec89a7bc3021ed446b8f20658b6ef3c5cae00dafd7f82495b8b13f","markdown":"## Machines virtuelles\n\nExemple : Java\n\n```text\nSource Code\n↓\nIntermediate Code\n↓\nVirtual Machine\n↓\nExecution\n```\n\nAvantages :\n- Plus grande portabilité\n- Même programme sur différents systèmes d'exploitation"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"ebae14d1aeec89a7bc3021ed446b8f20658b6ef3c5cae00dafd7f82495b8b13f","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Understanding Machine Instructions\n\n### Data Movement\n\n```text\nLOAD\nSTORE\nMOVE\n```\n\n### Arithmetic Operations\n\n```text\nADD\nSUBTRACT\nMULTIPLY\n```\n\n### Comparisons\n\n```text\nCOMPARE\n```\n\n### Control Instructions\n\n```text\nJUMP\n```","output":"","result":"## Understanding Machine Instructions\n\n### Data Movement\n\n```text\nLOAD\nSTORE\nMOVE\n```\n\n### Arithmetic Operations\n\n```text\nADD\nSUBTRACT\nMULTIPLY\n```\n\n### Comparisons\n\n```text\nCOMPARE\n```\n\n### Control Instructions\n\n```text\nJUMP\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3383-understanding-machine-instructions\">\n<h1>Understanding Machine Instructions</h1>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3383-data-movement\">\n<h1>Data Movement</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">LOAD\nSTORE\nMOVE</pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3383-arithmetic-operations\">\n<h1>Arithmetic Operations</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">ADD\nSUBTRACT\nMULTIPLY</pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3383-comparisons\">\n<h1>Comparisons</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">COMPARE</pre>\n</section>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3383-control-instructions\">\n<h1>Control Instructions</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">JUMP</pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2c68761833d5c29bbcea67aaf42108c870c82e9b90dcadbb002b6ba89dfd1b7b","markdown":"## Comprendre les instructions machine\n\n### Déplacement de données\n\n```text\nLOAD\nSTORE\nMOVE\n```\n\n### Opérations arithmétiques\n\n```text\nADD\nSUBTRACT\nMULTIPLY\n```\n\n### Comparaisons\n\n```text\nCOMPARE\n```\n\n### Instructions de contrôle\n\n```text\nJUMP\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"2c68761833d5c29bbcea67aaf42108c870c82e9b90dcadbb002b6ba89dfd1b7b","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Example: Adding Two Numbers\n\nGoal:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nProcessor instructions:\n\n```text\nLOAD 5\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```text\nRESULT = 8\n```","output":"","result":"## Example: Adding Two Numbers\n\nGoal:\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nProcessor instructions:\n\n```text\nLOAD 5\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nResult:\n\n```text\nRESULT = 8\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3384-example-adding-two-numbers\">\n<h1>Example: Adding Two Numbers</h1>\n<p>Goal:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">5 + 3</pre>\n<p>Processor instructions:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">LOAD 5\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT</pre>\n<p>Result:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">RESULT = 8</pre>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"593264f784bd39029b8bcceace9c368d29c6dc4760c6ac05181ba6fbed1afeab","markdown":"## Exemple : Addition de deux nombres\n\nObjectif :\n\n```text\n5 + 3\n```\n\nInstructions du processeur :\n\n```text\nLOAD 5\nLOAD 3\nADD\nSTORE RESULT\n```\n\nRésultat :\n\n```text\nRESULT = 8\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"593264f784bd39029b8bcceace9c368d29c6dc4760c6ac05181ba6fbed1afeab","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Conditional Execution\n\n```text\nIF temperature > 30\nTHEN turn on fan\n```\n\nImplementation:\n\n```text\nCOMPARE temperature, 30\nJUMP_IF_GREATER turn_on_fan\n```","output":"","result":"## Conditional Execution\n\n```text\nIF temperature > 30\nTHEN turn on fan\n```\n\nImplementation:\n\n```text\nCOMPARE temperature, 30\nJUMP_IF_GREATER turn_on_fan\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3385-conditional-execution\">\n<h1>Conditional Execution</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">IF temperature &gt; 30\nTHEN turn on fan</pre>\n<p>Implementation:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">COMPARE temperature, 30\nJUMP_IF_GREATER turn_on_fan</pre>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1628eb242eb40aaa65740a2ad916637ede058dca420d86ac782ae333e1eb5ef5","markdown":"## Exécution conditionnelle\n\n```text\nIF temperature > 30\nTHEN turn on fan\n```\n\nImplémentation :\n\n```text\nCOMPARE temperature, 30\nJUMP_IF_GREATER turn_on_fan\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1628eb242eb40aaa65740a2ad916637ede058dca420d86ac782ae333e1eb5ef5","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Repetition and Loops\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nCount from 1 to 10\n```\n\nConceptual loop:\n\n```text\nPRINT NUMBER\nINCREMENT NUMBER\nJUMP TO START\n```","output":"","result":"## Repetition and Loops\n\nExample:\n\n```text\nCount from 1 to 10\n```\n\nConceptual loop:\n\n```text\nPRINT NUMBER\nINCREMENT NUMBER\nJUMP TO START\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3386-repetition-and-loops\">\n<h1>Repetition and Loops</h1>\n<p>Example:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Count from 1 to 10</pre>\n<p>Conceptual loop:</p>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">PRINT NUMBER\nINCREMENT NUMBER\nJUMP TO START</pre>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8be1435e7680e4eef4b74cf6bc1edf9190c68ceb5b42bdb63a541984146da028","markdown":"## Répétition et boucles\n\nExemple :\n\n```text\nCount from 1 to 10\n```\n\nBoucle conceptuelle :\n\n```text\nPRINT NUMBER\nINCREMENT NUMBER\nJUMP TO START\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"8be1435e7680e4eef4b74cf6bc1edf9190c68ceb5b42bdb63a541984146da028","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Why Understanding Machine Code Matters\n\nUnderstanding machine instructions helps explain:\n- How software controls hardware\n- Why programming languages exist\n- Why computers execute instructions sequentially\n- How programming concepts map onto processor operations\n\n### Mental Model\n\n```text\nProblem\n↓\nAlgorithm\n↓\nSource Code\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nProcessor\n```","output":"","result":"## Why Understanding Machine Code Matters\n\nUnderstanding machine instructions helps explain:\n- How software controls hardware\n- Why programming languages exist\n- Why computers execute instructions sequentially\n- How programming concepts map onto processor operations\n\n### Mental Model\n\n```text\nProblem\n↓\nAlgorithm\n↓\nSource Code\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nProcessor\n```","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3387-why-understanding-machine-code-matters\">\n<h1>Why Understanding Machine Code Matters</h1>\n<p>Understanding machine instructions helps explain:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>How software controls hardware</li>\n<li>Why programming languages exist</li>\n<li>Why computers execute instructions sequentially</li>\n<li>How programming concepts map onto processor operations</li>\n</ul>\n<section data-type=\"sect2\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3387-mental-model\">\n<h1>Mental Model</h1>\n<pre data-type=\"program-listing\" data-code-language=\"text\">Problem\n↓\nAlgorithm\n↓\nSource Code\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nProcessor</pre>\n</section>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"84ac7bbffa49920f86484a41988651079b3c9cc681a3d4b414ae2602f6b2a464","markdown":"## Pourquoi la compréhension du langage machine est importante\n\nComprendre les instructions machine permet d'expliquer :\n- Comment le logiciel contrôle le matériel\n- Pourquoi les langages de programmation existent\n- Pourquoi les ordinateurs exécutent les instructions séquentiellement\n- Comment les concepts de programmation correspondent aux opérations du processeur\n\n### Modèle mental\n\n```text\nProblem\n↓\nAlgorithm\n↓\nSource Code\n↓\nMachine Code\n↓\nProcessor\n```"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"84ac7bbffa49920f86484a41988651079b3c9cc681a3d4b414ae2602f6b2a464","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Summary\n\n- Software consists of instructions executed by hardware.\n- Software can be divided into system software, applications, and libraries.\n- Programs implement algorithms.\n- High-level languages make programming easier for humans.\n- Source code must be translated into machine code.\n- Machine code is the language executed by processors.\n- Assembly language is a readable representation of machine instructions.\n- Compilers translate programs before execution.\n- Interpreters translate programs during execution.\n- Processors execute instructions such as loading, storing, calculating, comparing, and jumping.\n- Programming languages ultimately control hardware through machine instructions.","output":"","result":"## Summary\n\n- Software consists of instructions executed by hardware.\n- Software can be divided into system software, applications, and libraries.\n- Programs implement algorithms.\n- High-level languages make programming easier for humans.\n- Source code must be translated into machine code.\n- Machine code is the language executed by processors.\n- Assembly language is a readable representation of machine instructions.\n- Compilers translate programs before execution.\n- Interpreters translate programs during execution.\n- Processors execute instructions such as loading, storing, calculating, comparing, and jumping.\n- Programming languages ultimately control hardware through machine instructions.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3388-summary\">\n<h1>Summary</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>Software consists of instructions executed by hardware.</li>\n<li>Software can be divided into system software, applications, and libraries.</li>\n<li>Programs implement algorithms.</li>\n<li>High-level languages make programming easier for humans.</li>\n<li>Source code must be translated into machine code.</li>\n<li>Machine code is the language executed by processors.</li>\n<li>Assembly language is a readable representation of machine instructions.</li>\n<li>Compilers translate programs before execution.</li>\n<li>Interpreters translate programs during execution.</li>\n<li>Processors execute instructions such as loading, storing, calculating, comparing, and jumping.</li>\n<li>Programming languages ultimately control hardware through machine instructions.</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"709d64f30b4b412d0a3dc6825897b3e4dc3ae88742953caa29f9152c504377a9","markdown":"## Résumé\n\n- Le logiciel est constitué d'instructions exécutées par le matériel.\n- Le logiciel peut être divisé en logiciel système, applications et bibliothèques.\n- Les programmes implémentent des algorithmes.\n- Les langages de haut niveau facilitent la programmation pour les humains.\n- Le code source doit être traduit en code machine.\n- Le code machine est le langage exécuté par les processeurs.\n- Le langage assembleur est une représentation lisible des instructions machine.\n- Les compilateurs traduisent les programmes avant l'exécution.\n- Les interpréteurs traduisent les programmes pendant l'exécution.\n- Les processeurs exécutent des instructions telles que charger, stocker, calculer, comparer et sauter.\n- Les langages de programmation contrôlent en fin de compte le matériel par le biais d'instructions machine."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"709d64f30b4b412d0a3dc6825897b3e4dc3ae88742953caa29f9152c504377a9","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Key Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| Software | Collection of instructions executed by hardware |\n| System Software | Software that manages computer resources and hardware |\n| Application Software | Software designed to perform specific user tasks |\n| Library | Reusable collection of software components |\n| Algorithm | Step-by-step procedure for solving a problem |\n| Program | Implementation of an algorithm in a programming language |\n| Programming Language | Formal language used to write software |\n| Source Code | Human-readable program written by a programmer |\n| Machine Code | Binary instructions executed directly by a CPU |\n| Assembly Language | Human-readable representation of machine instructions |\n| Compiler | Program that translates source code into executable code |\n| Interpreter | Program that translates and executes source code |\n| Virtual Machine | Software layer that executes intermediate code |\n| Instruction Set | Collection of machine instructions supported by a processor |\n| Executable Program | Program ready to run on a computer |","output":"","result":"## Key Terms\n\n| Term | Definition |\n|---|---|\n| Software | Collection of instructions executed by hardware |\n| System Software | Software that manages computer resources and hardware |\n| Application Software | Software designed to perform specific user tasks |\n| Library | Reusable collection of software components |\n| Algorithm | Step-by-step procedure for solving a problem |\n| Program | Implementation of an algorithm in a programming language |\n| Programming Language | Formal language used to write software |\n| Source Code | Human-readable program written by a programmer |\n| Machine Code | Binary instructions executed directly by a CPU |\n| Assembly Language | Human-readable representation of machine instructions |\n| Compiler | Program that translates source code into executable code |\n| Interpreter | Program that translates and executes source code |\n| Virtual Machine | Software layer that executes intermediate code |\n| Instruction Set | Collection of machine instructions supported by a processor |\n| Executable Program | Program ready to run on a computer |","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3389-key-terms\">\n<h1>Key Terms</h1>\n<figure data-type=\"table\">\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Term</th>\n<th>Definition</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Software</td>\n<td>Collection of instructions executed by hardware</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>System Software</td>\n<td>Software that manages computer resources and hardware</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Application Software</td>\n<td>Software designed to perform specific user tasks</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Library</td>\n<td>Reusable collection of software components</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Algorithm</td>\n<td>Step-by-step procedure for solving a problem</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Program</td>\n<td>Implementation of an algorithm in a programming language</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Programming Language</td>\n<td>Formal language used to write software</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Source Code</td>\n<td>Human-readable program written by a programmer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Machine Code</td>\n<td>Binary instructions executed directly by a CPU</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Assembly Language</td>\n<td>Human-readable representation of machine instructions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Compiler</td>\n<td>Program that translates source code into executable code</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Interpreter</td>\n<td>Program that translates and executes source code</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Virtual Machine</td>\n<td>Software layer that executes intermediate code</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Instruction Set</td>\n<td>Collection of machine instructions supported by a processor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Executable Program</td>\n<td>Program ready to run on a computer</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</figure>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1b798f84df643d680bd087bb159d62b89ea42861b5b6e27f41ae13a64e841723","markdown":"## Termes clés\n\n| Terme | Définition |\n|---|---|\n| Logiciel | Ensemble d'instructions exécutées par le matériel |\n| Logiciel système | Logiciel qui gère les ressources et le matériel de l'ordinateur |\n| Logiciel d'application | Logiciel conçu pour accomplir des tâches spécifiques de l'utilisateur |\n| Bibliothèque | Collection réutilisable de composants logiciels |\n| Algorithme | Procédure étape par étape pour résoudre un problème |\n| Programme | Mise en œuvre d'un algorithme dans un langage de programmation |\n| Langage de programmation | Langage formel utilisé pour écrire des logiciels |\n| Code source | Programme lisible par l'humain, écrit par un programmeur |\n| Code machine | Instructions binaires exécutées directement par un processeur |\n| Langage assembleur | Représentation lisible par l'humain des instructions machine |\n| Compilateur | Programme qui traduit le code source en code exécutable |\n| Interpréteur | Programme qui traduit et exécute le code source |\n| Machine virtuelle | Couche logicielle qui exécute du code intermédiaire |\n| Jeu d'instructions | Ensemble des instructions machine prises en charge par un processeur |\n| Programme exécutable | Programme prêt à être exécuté sur un ordinateur |"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"1b798f84df643d680bd087bb159d62b89ea42861b5b6e27f41ae13a64e841723","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Review Questions\n\n- What is the difference between hardware and software?\n- What is the role of system software?\n- Give three examples of application software.\n- What is an algorithm?\n- What is the relationship between an algorithm and a program?\n- Why do programmers use high-level languages instead of machine code?\n- What is source code?\n- Why must source code be translated before execution?\n- What is the difference between machine code and assembly language?\n- What is the role of a compiler?\n- What is the role of an interpreter?\n- What are the advantages and disadvantages of compiled languages?\n- What are the advantages and disadvantages of interpreted languages?\n- What is a virtual machine?\n- Describe the path from a programming problem to CPU execution.\n- What types of instructions can a processor execute?\n- How can conditional execution be implemented using machine instructions?\n- Why is understanding machine code useful for computer scientists and engineers?","output":"","result":"## Review Questions\n\n- What is the difference between hardware and software?\n- What is the role of system software?\n- Give three examples of application software.\n- What is an algorithm?\n- What is the relationship between an algorithm and a program?\n- Why do programmers use high-level languages instead of machine code?\n- What is source code?\n- Why must source code be translated before execution?\n- What is the difference between machine code and assembly language?\n- What is the role of a compiler?\n- What is the role of an interpreter?\n- What are the advantages and disadvantages of compiled languages?\n- What are the advantages and disadvantages of interpreted languages?\n- What is a virtual machine?\n- Describe the path from a programming problem to CPU execution.\n- What types of instructions can a processor execute?\n- How can conditional execution be implemented using machine instructions?\n- Why is understanding machine code useful for computer scientists and engineers?","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3390-review-questions\">\n<h1>Review Questions</h1>\n<ul>\n<li>What is the difference between hardware and software?</li>\n<li>What is the role of system software?</li>\n<li>Give three examples of application software.</li>\n<li>What is an algorithm?</li>\n<li>What is the relationship between an algorithm and a program?</li>\n<li>Why do programmers use high-level languages instead of machine code?</li>\n<li>What is source code?</li>\n<li>Why must source code be translated before execution?</li>\n<li>What is the difference between machine code and assembly language?</li>\n<li>What is the role of a compiler?</li>\n<li>What is the role of an interpreter?</li>\n<li>What are the advantages and disadvantages of compiled languages?</li>\n<li>What are the advantages and disadvantages of interpreted languages?</li>\n<li>What is a virtual machine?</li>\n<li>Describe the path from a programming problem to CPU execution.</li>\n<li>What types of instructions can a processor execute?</li>\n<li>How can conditional execution be implemented using machine instructions?</li>\n<li>Why is understanding machine code useful for computer scientists and engineers?</li>\n</ul>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"247abc038cc2d76cd8fe9085abe67fd7265a95d132ddd8288d1fefee2245e923","markdown":"## Questions de révision\n\n- Quelle est la différence entre le matériel et le logiciel ?\n- Quel est le rôle du logiciel système ?\n- Donnez trois exemples de logiciels d'application.\n- Qu'est-ce qu'un algorithme ?\n- Quelle est la relation entre un algorithme et un programme ?\n- Pourquoi les programmeurs utilisent-ils des langages de haut niveau plutôt que le code machine ?\n- Qu'est-ce que le code source ?\n- Pourquoi le code source doit-il être traduit avant l'exécution ?\n- Quelle est la différence entre le code machine et le langage assembleur ?\n- Quel est le rôle d'un compilateur ?\n- Quel est le rôle d'un interpréteur ?\n- Quels sont les avantages et les inconvénients des langages compilés ?\n- Quels sont les avantages et les inconvénients des langages interprétés ?\n- Qu'est-ce qu'une machine virtuelle ?\n- Décrivez le chemin allant d'un problème de programmation à l'exécution par le processeur.\n- Quels types d'instructions un processeur peut-il exécuter ?\n- Comment peut-on mettre en œuvre l'exécution conditionnelle à l'aide d'instructions machine ?\n- Pourquoi la compréhension du code machine est-elle utile pour les informaticiens et les ingénieurs ?"}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"247abc038cc2d76cd8fe9085abe67fd7265a95d132ddd8288d1fefee2245e923","language":"English"}},{"input":"## Transition to Lecture 6\n\nWe now understand how software is transformed into machine instructions that hardware can execute.\n\nHowever, modern software systems rarely consist of a single program operating in isolation. Most applications must interact with users, files, networks, and other programs while sharing computer resources efficiently.\n\nIn Lecture 6, we will study **operating systems**, the software layer that manages hardware resources, coordinates program execution, controls memory and storage, and provides the environment in which applications run.","output":"","result":"## Transition to Lecture 6\n\nWe now understand how software is transformed into machine instructions that hardware can execute.\n\nHowever, modern software systems rarely consist of a single program operating in isolation. Most applications must interact with users, files, networks, and other programs while sharing computer resources efficiently.\n\nIn Lecture 6, we will study **operating systems**, the software layer that manages hardware resources, coordinates program execution, controls memory and storage, and provides the environment in which applications run.","resultHTML":"<section data-type=\"sect1\" id=\"nb-SC612_Lecture05-c3391-transition-to-lecture-6\">\n<h1>Transition to Lecture 6</h1>\n<p>We now understand how software is transformed into machine instructions that hardware can execute.</p>\n<p>However, modern software systems rarely consist of a single program operating in isolation. Most applications must interact with users, files, networks, and other programs while sharing computer resources efficiently.</p>\n<p>In Lecture 6, we will study <strong>operating systems</strong>, the software layer that manages hardware resources, coordinates program execution, controls memory and storage, and provides the environment in which applications run.</p>\n</section>\n","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{"French":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a1abe08f1c4515c91e5957723a0d155dd48bc4974be6ed826d4eb5ee90e7dfed","markdown":"## Transition vers le cours 6\n\nNous comprenons maintenant comment un logiciel est transformé en instructions machine que le matériel peut exécuter.\n\nCependant, les systèmes logiciels modernes consistent rarement en un seul programme fonctionnant de manière isolée. La plupart des applications doivent interagir avec des utilisateurs, des fichiers, des réseaux et d'autres programmes tout en partageant efficacement les ressources de l'ordinateur.\n\nDans le cours 6, nous étudierons les **systèmes d'exploitation**, la couche logicielle qui gère les ressources matérielles, coordonne l'exécution des programmes, contrôle la mémoire et le stockage, et fournit l'environnement dans lequel les applications s'exécutent."}},"translationSource":{"format":3,"sourceHash":"a1abe08f1c4515c91e5957723a0d155dd48bc4974be6ed826d4eb5ee90e7dfed","language":"English"}}]